ios: online, a server that never answers the login

Online (docs/ONLINE.md) the game socket goes to a server the player added, and one can take the connection and
then send nothing: an Engine-TS whose login worker is not running, a proxy whose backend is down, something
else at that address. The login's first read then gives up after its 30 s timeout and rejects with the socket
still open, which login() did not count as an IO error: it rethrew, GameShell.run() has no catch around
mainloop(), and the client stopped for good on "Connecting to server...". Now any rejection with the socket is
an IO error: the socket is closed and the form says "Error connecting to server.", as for a refused connection
(the host's box then names the reason). The same login runs the reconnect after a lost connection. A socket that
is already closed (the upstream case, and every offline one) goes the way it always did.

diff --git a/src/client/Client.ts b/src/client/Client.ts
index 0d90d36..5a79bcf 100644
--- a/src/client/Client.ts
+++ b/src/client/Client.ts
@@ -2221,6 +2221,12 @@ export class Client extends GameShell {
                 // IO error
                 this.loginMes1 = '';
                 this.loginMes2 = 'Error connecting to server.';
+            } else if (e instanceof WebSocket) {
+                // custom (ios): a server that took the connection and never answered (the read's 30 s timeout rejects with
+                // the socket still open): an IO error too, the socket closed, where upstream rethrows and its loop ends
+                this.stream?.close();
+                this.loginMes1 = '';
+                this.loginMes2 = 'Error connecting to server.';
             } else {
                 // exceptions in Java get stuck permanently on "Connecting to server..."
